ratorname{sin}⁡({315}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63a03dda-1f79-54bd-8fde-67abfc008cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63a03dda-1f79-54bd-8fde-67abfc008cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564614} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4c7d41-9d91-55af-a829-2d44cb358552" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fca26e85-1a1e-5672-a486-f4d949c36d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca26e85-1a1e-5672-a486-f4d949c36d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564653} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e994e7b-c5b3-51a5-bc01-6069ba4346c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a830f9c3-0121-5788-b38e-170711f9179f" :question/problem "If the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $2\\sqrt{3},$ and that $P$ makes an angle of ${240}^{∘}$ with the positive $x$-axis, then the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are$\\,(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=2\\sqrt{3},\\,\\theta ={240}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({240}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({240}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\sqrt{3},-3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2442c3e4-6efc-5e15-89f6-7d2d57190032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564604} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1385f2-403d-5b5e-96cd-323ad27d5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564608} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef219a0-8020-5eec-87fe-43e0abef3ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564610} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca1a3c5-4637-51a8-82a3-9937d8eddb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564618} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6134d2-8694-5624-a3fc-ee67d2bcafca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3